      feat(dart): promote to GA with type/import equivalences
      
      Vendors the wrapper-grammar fixes from ocaml-tree-sitter-semgrep#600
      (semgrep_dot_ellipsis_selector, semgrep_statement_list, class-body and
      top-level ellipsis arms) directly into this repo now that
      libs/ocaml-tree-sitter-semgrep is in-tree rather than a submodule, and
      regenerates languages/dart/tree-sitter/semgrep-dart from it.
      
      On top of that, closes the remaining GA gaps for Dart from PR #11735:
      - Typing.ml: && / || are boolean-typed for Dart (spec 17.21).
      - Parse_dart_tree_sitter.ml: populate id_info.id_type on typed locals
        and class fields so Naming_AST propagates types to use sites.
      - Naming_AST.ml / Naming_utils.ml: canonicalize Dart import segments
        (dart_canonical_segments) so patterns written against a library's
        conventional prefix match code that imports it under any alias.
      - Unit_engine.ml: Dart moves to the GA maturity tier.
      
      Includes fixture coverage under tests/patterns/dart, tests/parsing/dart,
      and tests/rules, plus a refresh of 4 parsing snapshots whose only diff
      was an unrelated id_svalue representation change already on develop.
      
      Ports semgrep/semgrep#11735 (by AlexLaroche) onto the post-sync in-tree
      grammar workflow, per malaverdiere's guidance on that PR: rebase, fold
      in the ocaml-tree-sitter-semgrep#600 companion change, regenerate.
      
